      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Elsevier Ireland Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Flow-limiting aorto-ostial coronary lesions are clinically important because they subtend a large myocardial territory and may induce extensive myocardial ischemia. Diagnosis and treatment of these lesions is challenging and procedural success and clinical outcomes are inferior to non-ostial lesions. The purpose of this review is to summarize current knowledge regarding aorto-ostial percutaneous coronary intervention and to suggest novel approaches for optimizing these procedures."
      },
